NetPi maintenance notes -- updated 2026-10-11
===========================================

Start with CONTRIBUTING.md for current build, test and regeneration commands.
STYLEGUIDE contains the inherited C conventions. The upstream HACKING document
is preserved verbatim in doc/upstream/HACKING as historical reference.

Encoder layout
--------------

include/lame.h is the public API. Public settings are handled in
libmp3lame/set_get.c. libmp3lame/lame.c validates and initializes a session,
converts input PCM, manages buffers and calls lame_encode_mp3_frame().
libmp3lame/encoder.c coordinates the psychoacoustic analysis, MDCT,
quantization and bitstream output. The corresponding implementations live in
psymodel.c, newmdct.c, quantize.c, vbrquantize.c and bitstream.c.
frontend/ contains the command line front end; changing an internal function
does not automatically require a new public API option.

State and allocation ownership
------------------------------

lame_global_flags holds public settings and refers to lame_internal_flags,
which holds the session's working state. Preserve that separation when adding
an option. A caller must successfully complete lame_init_params() before
encoding. Check all allocation results and propagate errors to the public
entry point instead of relying on assertions for out-of-memory handling.

Initialization failure must leave the object safe to close and retry.
free_init_data() unwinds derived initialization resources; freegfc() releases
the complete internal state. Resampler tables are prepared during session
initialization before PCM or output bytes are consumed. ReplayGain storage is
allocated only when the feature is requested. New resources need a matching
cleanup path and allocation-failure regression coverage.

Concurrency
-----------

Separate sessions still share legacy quantization and log-table initialization
within a process. This fork does not guarantee concurrent instance setup is
thread-safe. A lock around only lame_init() is insufficient: setup also occurs
in lame_init_params(), and table writes must not race with another encoder
using those tables. NetPi uses separate FFmpeg processes per conversion.

Avoid introducing new writable global state. Changing existing shared tables
requires a separate concurrency design and floating-point equivalence tests.

Validation
----------

Use the fork regression commands in CONTRIBUTING.md. The historical upstream
make test target compares an encoded fixture with a reference byte stream; it
is not a listening-quality test or the complete fork regression suite.

Changes to psychoacoustic, quantization, resampling or floating-point code need
representative audio testing as well as bounds, decode and sanitizer checks.
Report actual device measurements separately from QEMU execution. Keep native
CPU timing, temperature and listening results tied to the exact build and input.
